--TEST--
Reading an array element whose key is absent throws, where PHP warns and yields null — `rule:types/conversion` and `rule:types/absent-storage-is-never-a-zero-value`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:types/conversion`: nothing converts by itself, and there is no `null` to put in
// an `array<string>`. The present side of the bound first, so a case that
// threw everywhere would fail here rather than look right.
array<string> $a = ["x" => "y", "0" => "zero"];
echo $a["x"], "|", $a["0"], "\n";

// An `int` subscript names the same entry as its decimal (§ 5), and travels
// unrendered — the absent half of that pair is asserted below.
int $zero = 0;
echo $a[$zero], "\n";

// § 7 row 11: the throw is an ordinary `Throwable`, so it is catchable where
// it is written rather than a warning nothing observes.
try {
    echo $a["nope"], "\n";
} catch (Throwable $absent) {
    echo "absent: ", $absent->message, "\n";
}
try {
    int $seven = 7;
    echo $a[$seven], "\n";
} catch (Throwable $absentIndex) {
    echo "absent: ", $absentIndex->message, "\n";
}

// A stored `null` is not an absent key: `array<?string>` holds one legally,
// and reading it back is not the error above. Read bare, because `??` is the
// one guard row 11 is carved out of and would answer both alike — that half is
// `a-coalesce-guards-a-subscript-against-an-absent-key`.
array<?string> $maybe = ["k" => null, "j" => "here"];
?string $stored = $maybe["k"];
?string $present = $maybe["j"];
if ($stored == null) {
    echo "stored-null";
}
echo "|";
if ($present != null) {
    echo "here";
}
echo "\n";
try {
    echo $maybe["gone"], "\n";
} catch (Throwable $absentNullable) {
    echo "absent: ", $absentNullable->message, "\n";
}

// Every level of a nested read asks the question separately.
array<array<string>> $grid = ["r" => ["c" => "v"]];
echo $grid["r"]["c"], "\n";
try {
    echo $grid["r"]["gone"], "\n";
} catch (Throwable $absentInner) {
    echo "absent: ", $absentInner->message, "\n";
}
try {
    echo $grid["gone"]["c"], "\n";
} catch (Throwable $absentOuter) {
    echo "absent: ", $absentOuter->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
y|zero
zero
absent: undefined array key `nope`
absent: undefined array key `7`
stored-null|here
absent: undefined array key `gone`
v
absent: undefined array key `gone`
absent: undefined array key `gone`
